            <ArticleTitle>Symptomatic os infranaviculare.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>152-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4055/cios.2013.5.2.152</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The author observed a new accessory bone of the foot in the distal portion of navicular, which articulated with the medial cuneiform and the intermediate cuneiform, and named it os infranaviculare. A degenerative change was observed between the accessory bone and the navicular; this caused midfoot pain to the patient during weight-bearing. Thus, the patient was treated by excision of the accessory bone. The symptom was relieved at one-year postoperative.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
